{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790441899,"nonce":"6YBdIvBj2Zz6IOea9YpFVb/4lXg=","title":"AOT calls go through generic dispatch","message":"With the JIT pipeline in AOT, loops no longer dominate; every method call, getter and setter still goes through wren_call_N. Native AOT vs tiered JIT on the bench programs (arm64, one run each): fib 0.044s vs 0.0087s, method_call 0.018 vs 0.013, nbody 0.68 vs 0.076, mandelbrot 0.27 vs 0.020, binary_trees 0.41 vs 0.14, delta_blue 0.094 vs 0.062.\n\nThe JIT closes this with inline caches, CHA-driven direct calls and inlining of small bodies (inline_known). AOT has a whole-program method table (build_cha) but no inlining, and the LLVM AOT mode sends every call through the generic helper. Next: direct calls and inlining from the AOT CHA, in both the Cranelift and LLVM AOT lowerings.","files":null}]}